From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Strix Halo Packaging <packaging@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ROCm: refresh local carry for vLLM 0.30.0

Re-port of the 0.21.0 carry onto v0.30.0 (ced6857a). Kept sections:

- setup.py: forward CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS/HIPFLAGS into the CMake ROCm lane.
- csrc/libtorch_stable/cuda_vec_utils.cuh (moved from csrc/): vllm_bfloat16
  aliases for HIP.
- CLI: metadata-only `vllm --version`, lazy subcommand loading, and an
  import-light serve/utils/api_utils.py so plain `vllm --help` stays off
  arg_utils, chat_utils, transformers and the serve runtime.
- SageMaker optional in serve/sagemaker/api_router.py (moved) and
  serve/lora/api_router.py.
- TorchAO: metadata-only torchao_version_at_least (torchao_utils.py) and
  lazy TorchAOConfig registration.
- Qwen3.5/GDN: AMD autotune restriction and float32 gate exponent in
  third_party/flash_linear_attention/ops (moved from layers/fla/ops).
- FlashAttention CK/direct varlen interface gate (fa_utils, flash_attn).
- ROCm Triton unified-attention large-head prefill tile size.
- ROCm large-vocabulary top-k/top-p PyTorch fallback.
- Padded EAGLE/MTP drafter valid_count dtype.

Dropped as upstream-equivalent, obsolete with Triton 3.8, or AITER-only:
hipify byproduct copy, CLI lazy exports, arg_utils/protocol laziness,
gfx1x AITER enablement, Gemma 4 AITER preference, hybrid AITER exclusion
and realignment, AITER unified-attention block size, amdsmi warning,
FA Triton availability, vendored triton_kernels gate, Triton knobs guard.

